{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDExLS0yMDE1L0hhbm5haCUyMEFyZW5kdCUyMCUyODIwMTIlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Hannah Arendt","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/kB4hUbhIYmx7Xdpo1DGn15pstO3.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/li3pr2ZQjmrYuX4YWAPKvU8JaWc.jpg","description":"A portrait of the genius that shook the world with her discovery of “the banality of evil.” After she attends the Nazi Adolf Eichmann’s trial in Jerusalem, Arendt dares to write about the Holocaust in terms no one has ever heard before. Her work instantly provokes a furious scandal, and Arendt stands strong as she is attacked by friends and foes alike. But as the German-Jewish émigré also struggles to suppress her own painful associations with the past, the film exposes her beguiling blend of arrogance and vulnerability — revealing a soul defined and derailed by exile.\n\nRated NR · Released 11 Sept 2012 · Germany, France · Language: German · 113 min\nStudio: MACT Productions, Heimatfilm, Amour Fou Luxembourg\n\nOn your server — Audio: German","releaseInfo":"2012","genres":["Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.9","runtime":"113 min","cast":["Barbara Sukowa","Axel Milberg","Janet McTeer","Julia Jentsch","Nicholas Woodeson","Ulrich Noethen","Leila Schaus","Claire Johnston"],"director":["Margarethe von Trotta"],"released":"2012-09-11T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"Her ideas changed the world","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Margarethe von Trotta","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/rxFG8ZBtXRt0iRzMKiFOq579GD.jpg"},{"name":"Barbara Sukowa","character":"Hannah Arendt","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/lBPD683veT1RYdXqMAdAsldAtvI.jpg"},{"name":"Axel Milberg","character":"Heinrich Blücher","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/eK1Kkda8rOZMgo5BYBUVeYenOwj.jpg"},{"name":"Janet McTeer","character":"Mary McCarthy","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/qOKAI6aunD4J5MXiwwomAhI3jI2.jpg"},{"name":"Julia Jentsch